target: .github/workflows/ci.yml
verify: bash -c 'grep -qE "^ *for spec in .*Write:37" .github/workflows/ci.yml || { echo "the write parity gate has no floor"; exit 1; }'
expect: the write parity gate has no floor
why:    TestWriteMatchesThePython can go inert two ways CI would otherwise report green: the oracle unreachable, so every scenario SKIPs and go test counts a skip as success, or the scenario table emptied. The per-test floor catches both, but only while Write is in the floor loop. Anchored to the `for spec in` line for the reason the StorePath entry gives: an unanchored grep is satisfied by the comment above the loop, which names the Write floor too.
--- old
          for spec in Convergence:25 CycleCount:25 DroppedGates:28 StorePath:11 Write:37; do
--- new
          for spec in Convergence:25 CycleCount:25 DroppedGates:28 StorePath:11; do
